{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Blood flow-restricted exercise (BFRE) appears to hold considerable potential in spinal cord injury (SCI) rehabilitation, due to its ability to induce beneficial functional changes and morphological alterations from low-intensity, low-load exercise. However, it remains unclear if this training approach is feasible and safe in individuals with autonomic dysreflexia (AD). CASE PRESENTATION: A 23-year-old male with traumatic, cervical (C6), motor-complete (AIS: B) SCI and diagnosed AD completed eight sessions of BFRE for the upper extremities over 4 weeks. Blood pressure and heart rate recordings and perceptual pain responses were collected repeatedly during exercise. Blood samples were drawn pre- and post-training. Training was carried out in a neurorehabilitation hospital setting with appertaining medical staff readiness, and was supervised by a physiotherapist with expertise in AD in general as well as prior knowledge of the present patient's triggers and symptoms. Four incidences of AD (defined as systolic blood pressure increase >20 mmHg) were recorded across all training sessions, of which one was symptomatic. The patient's blood profile did not change considerably from pre- to post-training sessions. Self-reported average pain during training corresponded from \"mild\" to \"moderate\". DISCUSSION: The patient was able to perform 4 weeks of BFRE, but encountered episodes of AD. Similarly, two AD episodes were registered during a single conventional, free-flow resistance training session. Evidence from clinically controlled safety studies is needed in order to establish if and how BFRE can be applied in a rehabilitation strategy in SCI individuals with neurological level of injury at or above T6 level.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Krogh, Søren","Jønsson, Anette Bach","Vibjerg, Jørgen","Severinsen, Kåre","Aagaard, Per","Kasch, Helge"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023697"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Krogh, Søren"],"keyword":["Inclusion body myositis","Performance","Priorities","Resistance exercise","Spinal cord injury","vascular occlusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility and safety of 000000000004 weeks of blood flow restricted exercise in an individual with tetraplegia and known autonomic dysreflexia a case report","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7471262/pdf/41394_2020_Article_335.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-023697","identifier":[{"id":"85090164687","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000706365400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"32883956","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7471262","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-9795518b-8297-42af-9212-b498a34188ea","sdu-324303a9-78d6-4342-ac5a-07b644ba961f"],"keyword":["INCLUSION-BODY MYOSITIS","PERFORMANCE","PRIORITIES","RESISTANCE EXERCISE","SPINAL-CORD-INJURY","VASCULAR OCCLUSION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9038166F0C8DE5D94B6275A99F9A8C70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7471262/pdf/41394_2020_Article_335.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Spinal Cord Injury Centre of Western Danmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Viborg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Muscle Physiology and Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"424fd608-f85b-4165-bafd-2197370651c9","name":"Krogh, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette B","key":"jønssonpau","last":"Jønsson","locid":"c7824457-6c00-46b6-b131-364a3d4c519c","name":"Jønsson, Anette Bach","name_org":"Jønsson, Anette B","orcid":"0000-0002-7183-9175","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"vibjergpau","last":"Vibjerg","locid":"847b7be6-2ebe-4bce-ae33-82872429abad","name":"Vibjerg, Jørgen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaare","key":"severinsenpau","last":"Severinsen","locid":"2e5d4d8c-c0ae-4291-a1e0-c0da5e42c77c","name":"Severinsen, Kåre","name_org":"Severinsen, Kaare","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","locid":"8452f86e-3c45-4ec